orangeark (1.1.4-1) focal; urgency=low

  * OrangeArk: node tree auto-colours are now written into the tree model itself when a document loads, and a colour that came from the auto palette counts as "not customised" — previously a document saved by an older build kept its stored colour, so every node stayed the same colour and the feature looked like it did nothing
  * OrangeArk: colour palette relaid out OneNote-style — square swatches sitting shoulder to shoulder with a hairline gap (button padding/relief/focus padding stripped); theme colours run light→dark top to bottom, standard colours on one row; the Word-only gradient section is gone
